# Full feature archive: an ADDED requirement folded into an
# ALREADY-EXISTING capability (a brownfield spec.yaml source + its spec.md
# projection), so the record carries a real preImageSha, not the
# empty-image sentinel. want-auth-spec.md is the deterministic projection
# the fold + RenderProjection produces over the three requirements.

env HOME=/no-home

exec lifecycle archive 002-add-mfa
stdout 'seq 1  auth'

cmp openspec/specs/auth/spec.md want-auth-spec.md

grep '"op":"ADDED","requirement":"Multi-factor authentication"' openspec/ledger.jsonl
! grep '"preImageSha":"sha256:e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"' openspec/ledger.jsonl

-- lifecycle.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
consentPolicy: off

-- openspec/specs/auth/spec.yaml --
capability: auth
purpose: Authentication and session management for the product.
requirements:
  - name: Password login
    text: The system SHALL allow a registered user to authenticate with a username and password.
    scenarios:
      - name: Successful login with correct password
        given:
          - a registered user with a known password
        when:
          - the user submits the correct username and password
        then:
          - the system SHALL grant an authenticated session
  - name: Session expiry
    text: The system SHALL expire an authenticated session after 24 hours of inactivity.
    scenarios:
      - name: Session expires after inactivity
        given:
          - an authenticated session with no activity for 24 hours
        when:
          - the user makes a new request
        then:
          - the system SHALL require re-authentication

-- openspec/specs/auth/spec.md --
<!-- GENERATED by spec-lifecycle from spec.yaml — read-only projection, do not hand-edit. -->

# auth Specification

## Purpose

Authentication and session management for the product.

## Requirements

### Requirement: Password login
<!-- slug: password-login -->

The system SHALL allow a registered user to authenticate with a username and password.

#### Scenario: Successful login with correct password
<!-- slug: successful-login-with-correct-password -->

- **GIVEN** a registered user with a known password
- **WHEN** the user submits the correct username and password
- **THEN** the system SHALL grant an authenticated session

### Requirement: Session expiry
<!-- slug: session-expiry -->

The system SHALL expire an authenticated session after 24 hours of inactivity.

#### Scenario: Session expires after inactivity
<!-- slug: session-expires-after-inactivity -->

- **GIVEN** an authenticated session with no activity for 24 hours
- **WHEN** the user makes a new request
- **THEN** the system SHALL require re-authentication

-- openspec/changes/002-add-mfa/proposal.md --
# Add multi-factor authentication

## Why
Password-only login is insufficient for higher-security accounts.

## What Changes
- **auth:** ADDED - a second authentication factor requirement.

## Impact
- Extends the existing `auth` capability; no other capabilities affected.

-- openspec/changes/002-add-mfa/specs/auth/spec.yaml --
capability: auth
deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    requirement:
      name: Multi-factor authentication
      text: The system SHALL require a second authentication factor when MFA is enabled for an account.
      scenarios:
        - name: Login requires second factor when MFA is enabled
          given:
            - a user account with MFA enabled
          when:
            - the user submits a correct username and password
          then:
            - the system SHALL prompt for a second factor before granting a session

